\section{Feature Detection and Dispatch}\label{sec:abi-feature}

\subsection{CPU Feature Detection}\label{sec:abi-cpu-feature}

Modern processors support optional features (SIMD instruction sets, atomic
instructions, cryptographic extensions).  The ABI negotiation can incorporate
feature detection to select the best implementation:

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Compile-time detection:} The compiler knows the target
      architecture and generates code for the appropriate feature set.
\item \textbf{Run-time detection:} The program queries the CPU at run time
      (e.g., using \texttt{CPUID} on x86 or \texttt{getauxval} on Linux) to
      discover available features.
\item \textbf{OS-assisted detection:} The operating system provides feature
      information through auxiliary vectors or capability registers.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{IFUNC: Indirect Functions}\label{sec:abi-ifunc}

The GNU \texttt{IFUNC} (indirect function) mechanism allows a function's
implementation to be selected at load time:

\begin{verbatim}
  // Resolver function: selects the implementation
  void *resolve_dot_product(void) {
    if (has_avx512()) return dot_product_avx512;
    if (has_avx2())   return dot_product_avx2;
    return dot_product_generic;
  }

  // IFUNC declaration
  double dot_product(double *a, double *b, int n)
    __attribute__((ifunc("resolve_dot_product")));
\end{verbatim}

IFUNC provides a form of ABI negotiation at load time, but the selection is
fixed after loading---it cannot adapt to changing conditions.

\subsection{Dynamic Feature Dispatch}\label{sec:abi-dynamic-dispatch}

More flexible dispatch selects the implementation at each call, based on the
current state:

\begin{algorithm}[htbp]
\caption{Dynamic Feature Dispatch}\label{alg:abi-dispatch}
\begin{algorithmic}[1]
\Require Function $f$ with variants $\{f_1, \ldots, f_n\}$, caller context $C$
\Ensure Selected variant $f_i$
\For{each $f_i$ in preference order}
  \If{$C.\mathit{supports}(f_i.\mathit{requirements})$}
    \State \Return $f_i$
  \EndIf
\EndFor
\State \Return $f_{\mathit{fallback}}$
\end{algorithmic}
\end{algorithm}

